	(text_box "ADDRESSING IS NOT POSITIONAL, AND THAT MATTERS ON THE BENCH.\nThe bridge is at I2C 0x18.  The five probes have NO addresses to set: each DS18B20 carries a unique 64-bit ROM code lasered in at the\nfactory, and the DS2482's ROM Search walks the bus and finds all five.  So five on one bus is always electrically legal and can never\ncollide.\nWhat it does NOT tell you is WHICH probe is which.  Do it once at bring-up: read the five ROM codes, dunk one probe in ice water, read\nagain, and write the code on that probe's tail with a marker.  Then record the map in software.  Nothing on this board can do that for you."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.2400 142.2400 0)
		(size 214.6300 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
