	(text_box "WHY EVERY BRANCH HAS TWO 47R, AND WHAT DECIDES WHETHER FIVE IN PARALLEL ACTUALLY WORK.\nTHE BINDING LIMIT IS CAPACITANCE, NOT RESISTANCE.  DS2482 datasheet note 2: at STANDARD speed the total 1-Wire bus capacitance must not exceed 1 nF, and at OVERDRIVE 300 pF.  Budget: five DS18B20 DQ\npins at their specified 25 pF is 125 pF, the PCB is about 20 pF, which leaves 855 pF for five cables - about 170 pF each.  DROK specify the harness at 100 cm, and a 3-wire cable runs 60-100 pF/m, so\nthis bus is 445-645 pF: between 35 and 55 percent below the limit even at the pessimistic end.  IT FITS, with margin.  The ceiling would be about 1.7 m per probe, so do not extend these cables.\nRUN STANDARD SPEED ONLY.  Overdrive is arithmetically impossible here: the silicon and the bare PCB are already 145 pF against a 300 pF limit, before any cable.  Leave the DS2482's 1WS bit at 0.\nTHE 47R IN DATA damps the reflections off a five-way star, which is the topology 1-Wire likes least.  Its size is set by the worst LOW anyone has to read: with the DS18B20's specified VOL of 0.4 V at\n4 mA and the DS2482's weak pullup at its 1000 ohm minimum, 47R puts that low at 0.53 V.  The binding threshold is the DS18B20's own VIL of 0.8 V MAX - an absolute number, not a fraction of VDD, and\ntighter than the DS2482's VIL1 of 0.9 V - so 270 mV of margin.  100R would have left 136 mV.  Fit 0R if a probe will not enumerate.\nTHE 47R IN VCC stops one pinched cable pulling +3V3_D down and taking the Si5351, the helper clock and every measurement with it.  1.5 mA max while converting is 0.07 V of drop, leaving the probe at\n3.16 V against its 3.0 V minimum; a dead short is limited to 70 mA.  It is 1206 because that short puts 0.23 W in it.\nTP_1W IS HOW YOU CHECK ALL OF THIS.  Scope it during a conversion: the low should sit near 0.5 V and the rise should be well clear of the sample point.  Everything above is CALCULATED from the two\ndatasheets; only the cable capacitance is an estimate, and that is the one number this test point settles.\nOne spec corner, stated rather than hidden: the 0.07 V drop means DQ can idle up to 70 mV above the probe's own VDD, where the datasheet asks for VPU <= VDD.  It is far below a diode drop and only\nexists during the 750 ms conversion."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
